{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783162460,"nonce":"5EYtpk0gqyBp8fwCpgcE32eIpCU=","message":"Design amendment: Phase 4 (training compile) restructured into a three-rung risk ladder after evaluating and REJECTING a proposed 'Phase 3.5 forward-compiled training probe' (compile forward only, eager/manual backward). Rejection rationale, now recorded in the plan: (a) no such mode exists -- AOTAutograd fires on grad-enabled inputs, and a naive grad call OOMs by construction since the default partitioner saves every fetched weight (28 x ~0.9 GB); (b) the custom-autograd.Function bridge resurrects the hijack architecture this plan deletes and needs a throwaway eager re-fetch path; (c) it avoids only risks the Phase 0 spike already retired. Adopted ladder instead: Rung 1 (4-pre) = resident-block training compile (COMPILE_STREAMED_OFFLOAD Slice 2, now explicitly ordered first; isolates LoRA-in-joint-graph + _fp8_linear_training + checkpoint x compile at scale, zero streaming); Rung 2 (4a) = full-checkpoint streamed training, NO SAC (backward re-fetch from plain checkpoint recompute since fetch ops live inside the checkpointed callable); Rung 3 (4b) = SAC-min (MUST_RECOMPUTE fetches only, restores keep_last semantics). Each rung adds exactly one new variable and every line survives into the endpoint. INGRAPH_STREAM_PLAN.md updated (component 4, Phase 4, sequencing).","files":null}]}